WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:02.467
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.901
We hope you're doing well.

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:05.934
And now, if you don't mind,
let's get to the news.

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:10.434
Trump 2020 campaign lawyer
Jenna Ellis pleaded guilty today

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:11.667
to a criminal charge

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:13.734
in the Georgia election
interference case,

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:15.434
making her
former President Trump's

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:19.067
fourth codefendant of the trial
to plead guilty.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:21.901
So I guess in the end,
he did teach them all

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:23.167
the art of the deal.

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:25.300
[ Laughter ]
That's right.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.767
Jenna Ellis pleaded guilty
to a criminal charge

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:29.367
in the Georgia election case,
making her

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:32.767
Trump's fourth codefendant
of the trial to plead guilty.

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:36.167
You might remember
Ellis as the least weird lawyer

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:37.667
from this press conference.

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.701
She's the one sticking out
like a normal thumb.

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:47.434
She looks like Marilyn
from "The Munsters."

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:50.601
For the kids.
Got to put one of those...

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:55.033
It's 2023?

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:59.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:02.567
Michael Cohen is set to testify
today in a Manhattan courtroom

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:05.234
against former President Trump
in his civil fraud trial.

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:07.234
It's a big deal,
even though this picture

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:09.167
makes it look like
a "People's Court" case

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.434
about the property line
between two strip clubs.

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:15.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.801
At his rally in New Hampshire
last night,

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:18.701
former President Trump
appeared to mistake

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:22.467
the leaders of
Hungary and Turkey.

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:23.767
Hungary and Turkey.

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:25.601
You know, people come up to me
and they say,

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:28.367
"Oh, the Trump jokes
must write themselves."

00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:30.767
And usually I say, "No,
it's hard to write Trump jokes."

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:32.868
But then the guy gets on stage

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:34.200
and confuses
Hungary with Turkey

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.701
and I got to go, "Okay, yeah...

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:40.367
today, they write themselves."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:42.667
Republicans have nominated
Minnesota Representative

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:44.767
Tom Emmer for
speaker of the House,

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:46.501
but it remains to be seen

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:49.000
whether Emmer
can get past these "effers."

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:54.367
The House Freedom Caucus
yesterday

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:56.901
called on Republican lawmakers
to remain in Washington

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:58.968
until they're able to select
a new speaker.

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:01.601
Said Matt Gaetz, "Oh,
but I promised my girlfriend

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:02.934
we'd go trick or treating."

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:05.801
[ Laughter, audience groans ]

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:08.968
Texas Republic-- [ Chuckles ]

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:11.434
Texas Republican
Congressman Pete Sessions

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:13.367
said yesterday
that former President Trump

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:15.367
called him
about the speaker race

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:17.968
and said they had
a "polite conversation."

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:20.667
Um, eh, I hate to tell you,
but that wasn't him.

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:22.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.133
Trump having
a polite conversation

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:26.200
would be the clue
in an action movie

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.434
so the hero would know
which one to shoot.

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:29.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:33.767
Alabama Congressman
Gary Palmer announced

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:35.467
before today's
Republican conference meeting

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:37.767
that he has dropped out
of the race for speaker,

00:02:37.767 --> 00:02:40.601
though I'm not sure
that merited an announcement.

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:43.968
That's like calling Wendy's
to cancel your reservation.

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:46.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:50.334
A Kremlin spokesman today
dismissed longstanding rumors

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:53.133
that Russian President
Vladimir Putin uses body doubles

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:56.934
and said, "This evokes
nothing but a smile."

00:02:56.934 --> 00:03:00.634
And then he tried so hard
to smile...

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:02.133
that a little pee came out.

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:04.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:06.334
New York Mayor Eric Adams
announced yesterday

00:03:06.334 --> 00:03:08.734
that another
16,000 city employees

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:10.300
will be permitted
to work from home.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.467
Unfortunately,
they're all garbage collectors.

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:14.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:21.968
The Justice Department yesterday
filed a civil forfeiture claim

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:24.167
for a superyacht
reportedly belonging

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:26.067
to a sanctioned
Russian billionaire.

00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:28.167
"Hold up!
Let me disembark first,"

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:29.534
said Clarence Thomas.

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:31.367
[ Audience groans ]

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:34.968
According to a new report
from Uber Eats,

00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:36.934
the most frequently
paired food and alcohol

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:38.801
were ribeye steak and vodka.

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:41.667
Who did you poll --
The cast of "Mad Men"?

00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:43.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:45.200
Even a death row prisoner
would say,

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:48.767
"I don't know,
that sounds kind of heavy."

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.968
And finally,
Pepsi over the weekend unveiled

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:53.067
a new diner experience
in New York

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:55.868
to celebrate
its 125th anniversary.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:59.000
Because nothing captures
the diner experience

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.634
more than finding out
they only serve Pepsi.

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:04.267
And that was a monologue,
everybody!

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:07.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
We are off and running.

00:04:07.601 --> 00:04:09.501
I've got a great show
for you tonight.

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:11.934
He is a Grammy-nominated
stand-up.

00:04:11.934 --> 00:04:14.567
All of us here on the show
are big fans of his.

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:16.534
Shoemaker always
goes around saying

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:19.400
he's his favorite comedian,
even though I am right here.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.801 --> 00:04:22.033
He's hosting "SNL" this weekend

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:23.467
with musical guests
Foo Fighters,

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:25.300
so he's right
in the thick of it.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:26.334
I can't wait to talk to him.

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:28.234
Nate Bargatze is back
on the show.

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:30.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:30.934 --> 00:04:32.968
And he's one of our favorites.

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:35.634
He's back on Broadway
in "Gutenberg! The Musical!"

00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:37.534
at the James Earl Jones Theatre.

00:04:37.534 --> 00:04:39.567
He is one of the best
of all time.

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:41.467
Andrew Rannells
is going to be joining us.

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:44.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:46.334
And she is a brilliant author.

00:04:46.334 --> 00:04:47.667
She is a friend of this show.

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:50.300
She has a fantastic new novel,
"Let Us Descend."

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:53.801
It's out today.
Jesmyn Ward is back, everybody.

00:04:53.801 --> 00:04:55.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:59.400
During the old strike,

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.467
my brother and I
started a podcast.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.100
That's us as children.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.467
It's called "Family Trips
with the Meyers Brothers,"

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:08.033
and, boy oh boy, are we having
a grand old time doing it.

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:10.000
This week,
a new episode just dropped today

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.067
with our friend Jimmy Kimmel.

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:12.100
Right there,
there's Jimmy Kimmel.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.467
We talked
to Millie Bobby Brown,

00:05:14.467 --> 00:05:16.033
we talked to Leslie Jones.

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:17.901
Leslie Jones.

00:05:17.901 --> 00:05:20.968
If you're -- If you're
in the car with your kids

00:05:20.968 --> 00:05:22.601
and you want to listen
to a podcast

00:05:22.601 --> 00:05:24.601
where you talk to celebrities
about the family trips

00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:27.267
they took, don't listen
to the Leslie Jones one.

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:29.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:33.834
Haim, though, that was clean.

00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:36.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:39.634
Also, speaking of family
and speaking of home,

00:05:39.634 --> 00:05:42.601
I'm going back to my home
state of New Hampshire.

00:05:42.601 --> 00:05:45.968
I'm going to do a show
in Manchester, New Hampshire,

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:47.167
that's on November 4th.

00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:49.801
It's a Saturday
at the SNHU Arena.

00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:53.667
That's Southern New Hampshire
University Arena.

00:05:53.667 --> 00:05:54.901
And you know what?

00:05:54.901 --> 00:05:56.667
Shoemaker, you know
what it used to be called?

00:05:56.667 --> 00:05:59.067
The Verizon Arena. So...

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:01.033
I was pretty --
I was I was pretty bummed out

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:02.167
when they changed the name.

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:04.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.234 --> 00:06:07.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:09.200
Moving on, everybody.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:11.534
With 2024 just
around the corner,

00:06:11.534 --> 00:06:13.968
the race for president
is beginning to take shape.

00:06:13.968 --> 00:06:15.567
Which brings us
to a segment we call

00:06:15.567 --> 00:06:17.133
"Race for the White House."

00:06:17.133 --> 00:06:19.267
♪♪

00:06:20.868 --> 00:06:23.033
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.033 --> 00:06:24.133
You know, there was a real fear

00:06:24.133 --> 00:06:25.467
coming out
of the writers strike,

00:06:25.467 --> 00:06:28.434
"Hey, are they going to skimp
on graphic packages now?"

00:06:28.434 --> 00:06:30.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.834 --> 00:06:34.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.234 --> 00:06:36.868
It was recently reported that
polling from New Hampshire

00:06:36.868 --> 00:06:39.367
shows that Ron DeSantis
is currently in third place,

00:06:39.367 --> 00:06:40.634
with double digit support.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:42.567
This news is so good
for DeSantis,

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:44.634
it's enough to
make him weird smile.

00:06:44.634 --> 00:06:46.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.901 --> 00:06:49.267
-Leave him alone!

00:06:49.267 --> 00:06:50.300
-Excuse me?

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.300
-Leave him alone!

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:55.367
Haven't we made fun
of Ron DeSantis enough?

00:06:55.367 --> 00:06:57.434
-Yeah, well, you know,
it's just he's a public figure,

00:06:57.434 --> 00:06:59.133
so I think it's okay
to make jokes about him.

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:01.667
-Leave him alone!

00:07:01.667 --> 00:07:05.367
Poor guy.
He's just doing the best he can.

00:07:05.367 --> 00:07:07.300
The last thing he needs
after a long day

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:09.901
of telling everybody
they're woke is to get home,

00:07:09.901 --> 00:07:12.767
turn on the TV
and see you taking jabs at him.

00:07:12.767 --> 00:07:16.200
Leave him alone!

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.868
-I'm sorry. Are you
a Ron DeSantis supporter?

00:07:18.868 --> 00:07:20.801
-If I'm a supporter of anything,

00:07:20.801 --> 00:07:23.200
it's kindness, compassion,

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:26.200
not mean-spirited jokes.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:29.033
If you have to make fun
of somebody, make fun of me.

00:07:29.033 --> 00:07:30.868
-Yeah, I just
don't even know you.

00:07:30.868 --> 00:07:32.601
So why would I make fun of you?

00:07:32.601 --> 00:07:34.067
-Well, you could make fun
of the fact

00:07:34.067 --> 00:07:36.868
that I'm unable to pee
in public restrooms,

00:07:36.868 --> 00:07:39.267
but I can only poop in crowds.

00:07:39.267 --> 00:07:41.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:41.801 --> 00:07:43.334
-I don't want
to make fun of that.

00:07:43.334 --> 00:07:46.334
I usually just tell jokes about
people who are in the news.

00:07:46.334 --> 00:07:47.534
People like Ron DeSantis.

00:07:47.534 --> 00:07:50.033
-Oh, sure,
make fun of Ron DeSantis.

00:07:50.033 --> 00:07:51.267
Have your fun.

00:07:51.267 --> 00:07:53.133
Go ahead and say he looks
like a handsome man

00:07:53.133 --> 00:07:55.267
who's been stung
by a thousand bees.

00:07:55.267 --> 00:07:56.334
-Oh.

00:07:56.334 --> 00:07:58.567
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.567 --> 00:07:59.934
That's pretty harsh.

00:07:59.934 --> 00:08:03.601
-I know, so leave him alone!

00:08:03.601 --> 00:08:05.968
-I would like to get back
to my jokes, please.

00:08:05.968 --> 00:08:08.567
-Oh, you want something
to joke about? How about this?

00:08:08.567 --> 00:08:10.000
You could make fun
of the fact that

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:11.734
instead of having night terrors,

00:08:11.734 --> 00:08:15.434
I have day terrors
where I startle myself asleep.

00:08:15.434 --> 00:08:16.567
Aah!

00:08:19.767 --> 00:08:21.667
-Sir! Wake up!
-[ Stammering ]

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:22.834
Oh, leave him alone!

00:08:22.834 --> 00:08:25.400
[ Laughter ]

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:31.200
-I really don't want
to make fun of you.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.334
-Are you sure?

00:08:32.334 --> 00:08:33.868
Because you could
make fun of the fact

00:08:33.868 --> 00:08:35.901
that my teeth
are as soft as chalk,

00:08:35.901 --> 00:08:38.200
and my tongue is as hard
as a blackboard.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:41.634
And sometimes when I eat,
I accidentally do math.

00:08:41.634 --> 00:08:45.567
[ Laughter ]

00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:47.667
-Wow.

00:08:47.667 --> 00:08:49.501
-Don't you "wow" me.

00:08:49.501 --> 00:08:53.167
I'm the last person you want to
get into a wowing contest with.

00:08:53.167 --> 00:08:55.300
-A wowing contest?
-Yes.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:58.133
In high school,
I was the state "wow" champion

00:08:58.133 --> 00:08:59.767
three years running.

00:08:59.767 --> 00:09:01.300
-That's not a thing.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:02.667
-That's not a thing?

00:09:02.667 --> 00:09:09.534
Wo-o-o-o-ow!

00:09:09.534 --> 00:09:13.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:13.934 --> 00:09:17.701
Yes. Thank you.
-Just...

00:09:19.434 --> 00:09:20.934
-You want something else
to joke about?

00:09:20.934 --> 00:09:22.968
-No!
-Then how about this?

00:09:22.968 --> 00:09:24.501
You could make fun of the fact

00:09:24.501 --> 00:09:27.334
that my wife and I
have two kids.

00:09:27.334 --> 00:09:28.501
-Why would I make fun of that?

00:09:28.501 --> 00:09:30.200
-Well, the kids need to stay
on the farm

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.200
because our apartment
doesn't allow goats.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:33.734
-[ Groans ]

00:09:33.734 --> 00:09:36.133
-You see, baby goats
are called kids.

00:09:38.033 --> 00:09:39.300
-Don't fist bump him!

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:42.834
[ Laughter ]

00:09:42.834 --> 00:09:44.567
Sir, please,
just take your seat.

00:09:44.567 --> 00:09:46.000
-Oh, well, where would you
like me to take it?

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:46.868
To a different talk show

00:09:46.868 --> 00:09:48.334
where the host isn't mean?

00:09:48.334 --> 00:09:50.067
-I'd be fine with that.

00:09:50.067 --> 00:09:54.834
-Wo-o-o-ow-wow-wow-wow.

00:09:54.834 --> 00:09:57.534
If you want something
to joke about, joke about this.

00:09:57.534 --> 00:10:00.300
You can make fun of the fact
that I don't believe in tipping.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:02.634
I think you should
always use a condom.

00:10:02.634 --> 00:10:06.000
[ Laughter, audience groans ]

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.400
-Remember when you
all applauded his long "wow"?

00:10:11.667 --> 00:10:14.133
-I also call it my long "wow."
-Oh.

00:10:14.133 --> 00:10:16.200
[ Laughter ]

00:10:21.334 --> 00:10:22.467
-Stick to the cards!

00:10:22.467 --> 00:10:23.400
I --

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.133
[ Laughter ]

00:10:26.133 --> 00:10:28.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:28.834 --> 00:10:31.567
I'd really...

00:10:31.567 --> 00:10:34.801
I'd really like
to just continue my show.

00:10:34.801 --> 00:10:37.400
-Fine. Get back to
your Ron DeSantis jokes.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:40.100
But you know
what I'd say to that?

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:43.167
-Leave them alone?
-Leave them alone!

00:10:43.167 --> 00:10:47.234
[ Cellphone ringing ]
Oh. Oop. Sorry about that.

00:10:47.234 --> 00:10:48.934
My --
My kids are calling me.

00:10:48.934 --> 00:10:50.734
They need to be
picked up from school.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.901
[ Laughter ]

00:10:56.267 --> 00:11:00.267
[ Imitating goat bleating ]

00:11:07.834 --> 00:11:08.901
[ Coughs, clears throat ]

00:11:08.901 --> 00:11:10.767
Sorry. I had something
in my throat.

00:11:10.767 --> 00:11:14.634
I'll be there at three, kids.

00:11:14.634 --> 00:11:17.667
-So that sentence is
a lot longer in goat?

00:11:19.033 --> 00:11:20.200
-Yes.

00:11:21.734 --> 00:11:24.033
-Get out of here!
-Okay, I'll go.

00:11:24.033 --> 00:11:25.767
But remember, everyone:

00:11:25.767 --> 00:11:29.634
♪ There's room to be kind
if you just use your mind ♪

00:11:29.634 --> 00:11:33.367
♪ I must condone
you leave him alone ♪

00:11:33.367 --> 00:11:34.634
Wink!

